Feature exploration
===================

- Dark & Light mode colors
- Split up tinderbox-ng to a separate package

Bugs (evidence-based, found via tinderbox-ng compare)
=====================================================

- portage-ng silently no-ops install/merge for the top-level target.
  Reproducer:
    ssh root@vm-linux.local 'tinderbox-ng compare --build www-servers/apache'
  Symptoms:
    - portage-ng reports "Total: 16 completed" and
      "[step 9] OK   register www-servers/apache"
    - All 5 dependency packages land in VDB and on disk
    - The target itself (www-servers/apache-2.4.67) never appears in
      var/db/pkg and /usr/sbin/apache2 is missing
    - emerge in the parallel session merges all 6 packages including
      apache (auto-selects the prefork MPM via the apache eclass)
  Suggests register-without-merge for the chain-tail target.